# Ripknife agent workflow

## Commit tool changes

When you update Ripknife (code under `ripknife/`, `scripts/`, `tests/`, `Makefile`, `configs/`, `skills/`, or other tracked repo files), **commit to git as part of the workflow**. Do not leave substantial tool changes uncommitted unless the user explicitly says not to commit.

Before committing:

1. Run git from the repository root (the checkout that contains `ripknife/`).
2. Stage only repo/tool files — never runtime artifacts or secrets.
3. Use caveman-commit / Conventional Commits: `<type>(<scope>): <imperative summary>`, ≤50 chars when possible.

## Never commit

- `.venv/`, `output/`, `logs/`, ripped `*.mkv`, `.tmp/`
- Staging workflow artifacts under `staging/` (pending/ready/done/failed job files)
- Secrets: `.env`, `.env.*`, `*credentials*`, API keys
- The personal library checkout (`ripknife-configs` or `RIPKNIFE_CONFIG_DIR`)
- Generated per-disc manifests (`staging/`, and anything under `configs/` except `examples/`, `defaults.yaml`, `youtube.yaml`, `registry.yaml`)

## Working storage vs library

- The checkout is working storage: `output/`, `staging/`, `.tmp/` (`TMPDIR`)
- The library share is separate. Roots come from `site.env` in the personal config dir or from `RIPKNIFE_ANIME_NAS`, `RIPKNIFE_SHOWS_NAS`, and `RIPKNIFE_MOVIES_NAS`
- systemd file logs: `/var/log/ripknife`; ad-hoc `make watch-all`: repo `logs/`

## Config split

- Tool repo `configs/` holds examples and `defaults.yaml` only
- Generated manifests are gitignored here. The rip reads `staging/ready`
- When a manifest is generated, archive a copy in the sibling `ripknife-configs` checkout (`generated/`) for reference. Do not push that repo from the watcher
- Personal manifests, `youtube.yaml`, `registry.yaml`, and `site.env` live in `RIPKNIFE_CONFIG_DIR`, or in a sibling directory named `ripknife-configs` when that checkout exists
- One manifest per disc

## Multi-disc movies

- One manifest per disc; output name: `Title (Year) - Disc N.mkv`
- When stitching parts: set `post.copy_to_nas: false` on each disc manifest
- Rip discs independently; stitch runs post-rip via `ripknife/stitch.py` (rip-watcher hook)
- Copy **only the stitched file** to the library after join — not per-disc masters
- Non-theatrical cuts: set `output.edition` → Plex `{edition-…}` on masters and the stitched file

## Library mapping

- **Any cartoon or animation** (Western cartoon, Japanese anime, CG series, animated feature) → `Anime/`
- Animated **series**: `nas.share: /path/to/library/Anime/<Show>` (never Shows)
- Animated **movies**: `nas.movies: true` and `nas.share: /path/to/library/Anime/Movies` (Plex Movies-type library; a TV-type Anime library ignores root MKVs)
- **Live-action TV** only → `/path/to/library/Shows/<Show>`
- **Live-action movies** → `/path/to/library/Movies/`
- Do not move already-copied series; this is future mapping/rip output only

## Drives

- Slot-loading drives: `eject -t` fails. Do not tell the operator to close a tray.
- `eject -x` sets spindle speed. It does not close the slot. `eject -x 0` restores speed.
- Do not copy a bad or gapped file to the library.
